<title>CHINA: China's February cereal imports detailed.</title>
<headline>China's February cereal imports detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows the wheat, barley, corn and rice import figures of up to five major Chinese import offices as well as the country of origin in January and February.</p>
<p>Details were provided by the General Administration of Customs of China.</p>
<p>Figures are in tonnes. Percentages represent the share of the total market. Percentages may not add up to 100 percent as details of some smaller import regions and supplying countries have not been included.</p>
<p>------WHEAT</p>
<p> Feb imports:   110,250	 Jan-Feb  total imports: 274,146</p>
<p>  CUSTOMS	     Feb	    Pct	   Jan-Feb	Pct</p>
<p>    Fuzhou		0	    0.0	    15,459	5.6</p>
<p>    Dalian	 31,500	   28.6	    31,500     11.5</p>
<p>    Huangpu	     0	    0.0	    31,500     11.5</p>
<p>    Nanning	     0	   54.5	    89,250     32.6</p>
<p>    Nanjing	78,750			     78,750     28.7</p>
<p>ORIGINS</p>
<p>    Canada	110,250	  100.0	   236,250     86.1</p>
<p>    U.S.		  0	    0.0	    31,857     11.6</p>
<p>    Australia	   0	    0.0	     6,039	2.2</p>
<p>------BARLEY</p>
<p> Feb imports:    60,850	 Jan-Feb  total imports: 237,338</p>
<p>  CUSTOMS	     Feb	    Pct	   Jan-Feb Pct</p>
<p>    Nanjing	33,350	   54.8	    85,850     36.1</p>
